          {
            "title": "Intro",
            "id": 82582,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Spesso incontreremo diversi set di dati che dovremo combinare in uno solo, come il valore delle vendite durante il fine settimana.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"sales_sat = [\" /><text value=\"50\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"22\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"sales_sun = [\" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"9\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"11\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"40\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /></content></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Plus operator",
            "id": 82583,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Per combinare due dataset, come quelli in <code>dataset_1</code> e <code>dataset_2</code>, usiamo i nomi delle liste e l'operatore <code>+</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"dataset_1 = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"dataset_2 = [\" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(dataset_1 + dataset_2)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"48\" endIndex=\"57\" /><option startIndex=\"58\" endIndex=\"59\" /><option startIndex=\"60\" endIndex=\"69\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>dataset_1</code>, seguito da <code>+</code> e infine <code>dataset_2</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Usa <code>+</code> per combinare due liste. I valori della lista a sinistra precedono quelli della lista a destra.</p><p>Unisci i dataset in modo che il codice stampi <code>[4, 5, 1, 2, 3]</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"dataset_1\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"=\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"[\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\",\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\",\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"dataset_2\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"=\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"[\" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\",\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"dataset_2\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"+\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"dataset_1\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"48\" endIndex=\"57\" /><option startIndex=\"58\" endIndex=\"59\" /><option startIndex=\"60\" endIndex=\"69\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[4, 5, 1, 2, 3]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>dataset_2</code>, seguito da <code>+</code> e infine <code>dataset_1</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Appended at the end",
            "id": 82584,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Quando usi <code>+</code>, la seconda lista viene aggiunta alla fine della prima lista.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"dataset_1 = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"dataset_2 = [\" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(dataset_1 + dataset_2)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"58\" endIndex=\"59\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di digitare <code>+</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Different types",
            "id": 82585,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Possiamo anche usare <code>+</code> per combinare liste contenenti tipi di valori diversi, come il valore numerico <code>seats</code> e quello booleano <code>taken</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"seats = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"taken = [\" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"False\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(seats + taken)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"23\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 2, 3, True, True, False]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>seats</code>, seguito da <code>taken</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Puoi usare <code>+</code> per combinare liste contenenti tipi di valori diversi.</p><p>Unisci <code>seats</code> e <code>taken</code>, con seats per prima, per stampare <code>[1, 2, 3, True, True, False]</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"seats = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"taken = [\" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"False\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(seats + taken)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"53\" endIndex=\"58\" /><option startIndex=\"59\" endIndex=\"60\" /><option startIndex=\"61\" endIndex=\"66\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"*\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 2, 3, True, True, False]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>seats</code>, seguito da <code>+</code> e infine <code>taken</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Save in variable",
            "id": 82586,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Per riutilizzare l'elenco combinato, possiamo salvarlo in una variabile, come qui con <code>combined</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"dataset_1 = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"dataset_2 = [\" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"combined = dataset_1 + dataset_2\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(combined)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"50\" /><option startIndex=\"51\" endIndex=\"52\" /><option startIndex=\"53\" endIndex=\"74\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>combined</code>, seguito da <code>=</code> e infine <code>dataset_1 + dataset_2</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Unisci i due dataset, prima <code>dataset_1</code>, e memorizza il risultato in <code>combined</code>, in modo che il codice stampi <code>[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"dataset_1 = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"dataset_2 = [\" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"combined = dataset_1 + dataset_2\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(combined)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"50\" /><option startIndex=\"51\" endIndex=\"52\" /><option startIndex=\"53\" endIndex=\"62\" /><option startIndex=\"63\" endIndex=\"64\" /><option startIndex=\"65\" endIndex=\"74\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>combined</code>, seguito da <code>=</code>, <code>dataset_1</code>, <code>+</code> e infine <code>dataset_2</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Plus operator",
            "id": 82669,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Cosa fa l'operatore <code>+</code> quando viene usato su due liste?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Unisce gli elementi delle due liste in una nuova lista</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Aggiunge ogni elemento di una lista a ogni elemento dell'altra</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Unisce gli elementi delle due liste in una nuova lista.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Quale nuova lista crea <code>[1, 2] + [3, 4]</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>[1, 2, 3, 4]</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>[4, 6]</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>[[1, 2], [3, 4]]</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>[1, 2, 3, 4]</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Appended at the end",
            "id": 82670,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Quando scrivi <code>list_1 + list_2</code>, in quale ordine appariranno gli elementi nella nuova lista?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Gli elementi di <code>list_1</code> appariranno per primi, seguiti da quelli di <code>list_2</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Gli elementi di entrambe le liste saranno mescolati casualmente</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Gli elementi di <code>list_1</code> appariranno per primi, seguiti da quelli di <code>list_2</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Se <code>first = [\"A\", \"B\"]</code> e <code>second = [\"C\", \"D\"]</code>, che cosa crea <code>first + second</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>[\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\"]</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>[\"C\", \"D\", \"A\", \"B\"]</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>[\"A\", \"C\", \"B\", \"D\"]</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>[\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\"]</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Different types",
            "id": 82671,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Quali tipi di valori possono contenere le liste che combiniamo?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Qualsiasi tipo</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Solo lo stesso tipo</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Qualsiasi tipo.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Che cosa crea <code>[\"id\"] + [7, True]</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>[\"id\", 7, True]</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Provoca un errore perché i tipi di valore sono diversi.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>[\"id\", \"7\", \"True\"]</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>[\"id\", 7, True]</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Save in variable",
            "id": 82672,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Come possiamo riutilizzare la lista che otteniamo unendo due liste?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Lo salviamo in una variabile </item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Non possiamo riutilizzarlo, possiamo solo visualizzarlo una volta</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Lo salviamo in una variabile .</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Devi riutilizzare in seguito il risultato di <code>first + second</code>. Quale riga memorizza la lista unita?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>combined = first + second</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>print(first + second)</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>first + second</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>combined = first + second</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Plus operator ",
            "id": 82674,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Scrivi <code>+</code> per unire le due liste che memorizzano il tasso di crescita di una pianta.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"growth_rate_1 = [\" /><text value=\"0.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.7\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"growth_rate_2 = [\" /><text value=\"0.8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(growth_rate_1 + growth_rate_2)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"85\" endIndex=\"86\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[0.5, 0.7, 0.8, 0.8, 0.6, 0.6]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di digitare <code>+</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Appended at the end",
            "id": 82676,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Unisci le liste <code>customers</code> e <code>order_number</code> in modo che i nomi dei clienti vengano prima.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"customers = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Jess&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Mike&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Lynn&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"order_number = [\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(customers + order_number)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"69\" endIndex=\"78\" /><option startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"80\" /><option startIndex=\"81\" endIndex=\"93\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"['Jess', 'Mike', 'Lynn', 3, 1, 2]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>customers</code>, seguito da <code>+</code> e infine <code>order_number</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Unisci <code>customers</code> e <code>order_number</code> mettendo prima i nomi, in modo che stampi <code>['Jess', 'Mike', 'Lynn', 3, 1, 2]</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"customers = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Jess&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Mike&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Lynn&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"order_number = [\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(customers + order_number)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"69\" endIndex=\"78\" /><option startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"80\" /><option startIndex=\"81\" endIndex=\"93\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"['Jess', 'Mike', 'Lynn', 3, 1, 2]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>customers</code>, seguito da <code>+</code> e infine <code>order_number</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Different types",
            "id": 82675,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Unisci le liste <code>t⁠e⁠a⁠m⁠_⁠1</code> e <code>t⁠e⁠a⁠m⁠_⁠2</code> in modo che i nomi dei giocatori e i punteggi vengano stampati in un'unica lista.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"team_1 = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Ana&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"78\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Joe&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"team_2 = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Kim&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"57\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sam&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(team_1 + team_2)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"78\" endIndex=\"79\" /><option startIndex=\"80\" endIndex=\"86\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"['Ana', 78, 'Joe', 80, 'Kim', 57, 'Sam', 60]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>+</code>, seguito da <code>team_2</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Unisci <code>team_1</code> e <code>team_2</code> in una lista, prima team_1, in modo che il codice stampi <code>['Ana', 78, 'Joe', 80, 'Kim', 57, 'Sam', 60]</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"team_1 = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Ana&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"78\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Joe&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"team_2 = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Kim&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"57\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sam&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(team_1 + team_2)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"71\" endIndex=\"77\" /><option startIndex=\"78\" endIndex=\"79\" /><option startIndex=\"80\" endIndex=\"86\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"*\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"['Ana', 78, 'Joe', 80, 'Kim', 57, 'Sam', 60]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>team_1</code>, seguito da <code>+</code> e infine <code>team_2</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Save in variable",
            "id": 82677,
            "contentType": "interactive",
